   169	name: migrate-module
   170	description: Migrates one service module from callback-style database access to the matching repository class, then runs that module's tests. Use when the user names a single service file to migrate. Handles exactly one module per invocation.
   171	---
   172	
   173	# Repository pattern migration
   174	
   175	The mapping table from callback call to repository method:
   176	
   177	| Callback call in a service | Repository method |
   178	|---|---|
   179	| `query('users', u => u.deleted_at === null, cb)` | `UserRepository.findActive()` |
   180	| `query('users', u => u.id === id, cb)` | `UserRepository.findById(id)` |
   181	| `update('users', id, { deleted_at }, cb)` | `UserRepository.softDelete(id, when)` |
   182	| `query('orders', o => o.user_id === id ..., cb)` | `OrderRepository.findByUser(id)` |
   183	| `query('orders', o => o.status === 'paid' ..., cb)` | `OrderRepository.findPaid()` |
   184	
   185	The migration changes the module's exported functions from callbacks to promises, so
   186	the code that calls them has to change with them. You may edit only these files:
   187	
   188	- the target service file and its test file
   189	- the routes in `src/api/routes.js` that call the target's functions, and no other line there
   190	- `src/repositories/payment-repository.js`, when the target is `payment-service.js`
   191	
   192	If the migration needs a change anywhere else, stop and report the file and the reason
   193	instead of editing it.
   194	
   195	Steps:
   196	
   197	1. Read the target service file, its test file, and `src/api/routes.js`.
   198	2. Replace every direct `query`/`update` import and call with the matching repository method.
   199	3. Convert the exported functions to return promises. Update the test file to await them.
   200	4. Update each route that calls the target's functions so it waits for the promise and
   201	   passes the result or the error to the route's callback.
   202	5. Run the module's tests, `node --test tests/<module>.test.js`, and then
   203	   `node scripts/check-routes.js`. Both must pass.
   204	6. Stop after three failed attempts and report what blocked you.
   205	
   206	`payments` has no repository yet. If the target is `payment-service.js`, create
   207	`src/repositories/payment-repository.js` following the shape of the other two.
